          "source": "",
          "thread": "Bankruptcy creditor claim recovery",
          "why": "FTX and Celsius creditors receiving at or above par on distressed claims turned catastrophic collapses into an ongoing money story, with readers tracking real dollar recoveries across years of proceedings."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Protocol denial after exploit",
          "why": "When hacks or unexpected liquidations occur, readers click the official guarantee or denial — DMM Bitcoin pledging full repayment, Pac Finance blaming an unauthorized parameter change — because those assurances are the highest-stakes moment of any incident."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Pump-and-dump market structure claims",
          "why": "The Chainalysis finding that ERC-20 pump-and-dump attackers average only $2,672 challenged the dominant narrative that such schemes are highly profitable, making it a compelling counter-claim that reframes market manipulation as atomized noise."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Airdrop claim windows going live",
          "why": "Time-sensitive claim openings for LayerZero, ether.fi, and Orbiter Finance drive clicks because they carry immediate financial action — missing the window means missing tokens."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Insider wealth during regulatory reckoning",
          "why": "Forbes claiming CZ made billions while incarcerated captured the moral incongruity of crypto's enforcement era, merging celebrity finance with criminal justice in a single headline."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Legal and IP disputes against crypto",
          "why": "Telegram's court-ordered suspension, Unstoppable Domains patent claims against ENS, and the Kansas City Fed opposing Custodia's banking charter showed readers how incumbent institutions use legal claims as competitive weapons against crypto infrastructure."
        }
      ]
    },
